    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0642" n="616" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v09/pg616"/>

                <head>287. Letter From Secretary of Commerce Hodges to Secretary of State Rusk<anchor n="0" xml:id="d287-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-09-20">September 20,
                        1963</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am pleased to attach for
                    your information the report of the White House Conference on Export Expansion
                    which was held on September 17-18, 1963. For your convenience, I am also
                    attaching a summary which reflects the highlights of the reports of the several
                    Committees.</p>
                <p>The report is only a beginning. We plan to hold little “White House Conferences”
                    in all parts of the country starting next week so that the export expansion
                    story can be brought home to Americans everywhere.</p>
                <pb facs="0643" n="617" xml:id="pg617"/>
                <p>May I thank you once again for your cooperation and support. The enthusiastic
                    reports we have been receiving from members of the Conference on the way in
                    which it was conducted and the results which have been achieved are indeed
                    gratifying.</p>
                <p>We will now move forward promptly to develop appropriate action programs. I am
                    looking forward to your continued cooperation in this most important task.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Luther H.
                                Hodges</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d287-a1.xml" xpointer="d287-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
